@Tristan the model must be compiled on device, the pkl will only be generated validly if it’s on the device. Even if you manage to compile it on PC it will not work.

That being said, we don’t have an easy way for people to try to add their own model. I never thought of that 😂 

But on sunnypilot/models/fetcher.py you can change the driving_models.json url to something else. Whatever you point it to will be the new model list

@discountchubbs you had mentioned considering splitting the model chooser into sub menus for each family.

As the list of models keeps growing it is getting slower to find what you want.

How about a favorite checkbox next to models that you like. Then the top right of the chooser screen would have a button to select "View All" or "View Favorites"

yep - that's exactly what I'd expect that command to do 🙂  thanks for confirming.

@nayan I have another slightly-offtopic question while we're talking about the FS: Is there a way to pull an **entire drive** off of the c3 and have all the video segments combined into one video?

I've explored this before (I miss having fleet manager for this...), and I saw that drives are under `/data/media/0/realdata/000000b6--c775112a0f--[segmentID]/xcamera.hevc` . As far as I could tell, there was no easy way to combine all of these segments into one video.

@Gusdaz22 i think the lane positioning of SL2 is very consistent and it has a decent amount of torque. I have not seen many models as predictable as SL2, which is a quality that I enjoy a lot.

Steam Powered feels very smooth and a little bit more “human”-like to me. It sometimes hugs the edge of the lane and stuff though. More torque than DTR6 and SL2 I think.

DTR6 sometimes feels like it doesn’t keep a good lane position very well, especially in curves. it feels a little bit less “locked in” and more sloshy like i am riding a boat

